Furthermore, the results of the self-awareness questionnaire are presented in Table II, indicating that the participants’ actions during the experiments were not adversely influenced by simulation factors subjectively. Notably, all participants reported that their behavior was unaffected by simulation sickness, with a high average score (Mean of 4.11 on a 5-point Likert scale) reflecting their agreement that their intervention actions were spontaneous (Mean of 4.27). A majority of the participants (40 out of 46) rated the visualization and 3D effects of the simulation platform very highly, and all participants responded positively to the simulated futuristic scenarios. From a statistical perspective, the questionnaire achieved a Cronbach’s α value of 0.74, denoting good internal consistency in the participants’ positive responses.

